Package: adltools
Type: Package
Title: Teaching-Oriented Tools for Autoregressive Distributed Lag Models
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: person("Miguel A.", "Arranz", email = "maarranz@eco.uc3m.es",
    role = c("aut", "cre"),
    comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-5951-2284",
                affiliation = "Universidad Carlos III de Madrid"))
Description: Formulation, estimation and inference for autoregressive
    distributed lag (ADL) models, developed for Applied Time Series
    Econometrics (ATSE) at Universidad Carlos III de Madrid. Models can be
    written with 'dynlm'-style formulas or with lag orders, and the package
    brings together tests that are otherwise scattered across packages,
    starting with the direct (Sargent) Granger non-causality procedure with
    instantaneous causality and the eight-way classification of causal
    relations.
